<title>HUNGARY: Hungary Raiff.Unicbank taps $50mln, LIBOR+18.75bps.</title>
<headline>Hungary Raiff.Unicbank taps $50mln, LIBOR+18.75bps.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Raiffeisen Unicbank said on Friday it tapped the markets for a $50 million, five year syndicated loan at 18.75 basis points above LIBOR.</p>
<p>&quot;Currently this is the lowest interest under which a bank operating in Hungarian tapped international markets for loan,&quot; Raiffeisen Unicbank said in a statement.</p>
<p>The loan is provided by a consortium of banks, led by Germany's Deutsche Bank AG, it said.</p>
<p>Raiffeisen Unicbank will spend the loan to finance the medium and long-term development projects of its clients, it said.</p>
<p>-- Emese Bartha, Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
